steps.description:
With `onDemand`, zot checks a stored tag against upstream on each request. For tags that don't change once pushed, such as release versions, this check only adds latency, and the request fails or waits when the upstream is slow or unreachable.

As suggested in #4128, this is now a value of
```yaml
{
  "urls": ["https://index.docker.io"],
  "onDemand": true,
  "skipUpstreamIfLocal": true,
  "content": [
    {
      "prefix": "rancher/**",
      "tags": { "semver": true }
    }
  ]
}
```
